{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And that he is ruler.</b> — וַאֲשֶׁר הוּא מוֹשֵׁל:" "<b>And his heart went numb.</b> His heart shifted and withdrew from believing — his heart would not turn toward the matter. It is the language of מְפִיגִין טַעֲמָן in Mishnaic language, and like ״מֵאֵין הֲפֻגוֹת״ (Lamentations 3), and ״וְרֵיחוֹ לֹא נָמַר״ (Jeremiah 48) — they translate it וְרֵיחֵיהּ לָא פָג."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:38.884283635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}